entries[1301647] = { ["name"] = "Cursed Argentleaf", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nThe silverleaf of Quel'Thalas has grown more lustrous in recent years, gaining a unique sheen that allows anyone to recognize it at a glance. Because of these changes, this new offshoot of silverleaf has become known as argentleaf.\n\nRegularly found among other common foliage, it is a standard ingredient of many recipes and is thus highly sought after.\n\nThe herb gives off a sinister aura as if the very roots are laced with malice. Gathering the plant will surely bring some relief to the land, but at what cost to the herbalist?" }
entries[1301648] = { ["name"] = "Wounded" }
entries[1301649] = { ["name"] = "Cursed Azeroot", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nThe hearty earthroot plant has grown stronger in recent years. Difficult to gather, but just as potent in crafting, azeroot is key to many recipes in Quel'Thalas.\n\nThis sturdy wooden herb can be found on or around trees in the Quel'Thalas region.\n\nThe herb gives off a sinister aura as if the very roots are laced with malice. Gathering the plant will surely bring some relief to the land, but at what cost to the herbalist?" }
entries[1301650] = { ["name"] = "Wounded" }
entries[1301651] = { ["name"] = "Cursed Mana Lily", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nAnother recent offshoot species, mana lily is a new variant of mageroyal. The latent magic present in the Quel'Thalas region has seeped into the mana lily, giving them potent properties for crafting.\n\nIf you're ever gathering around bodies of water, you can expect to find mana lilies somewhere nearby.\n\nThe herb gives off a sinister aura as if the very roots are laced with malice. Gathering the plant will surely bring some relief to the land, but at what cost to the herbalist?" }
entries[1301652] = { ["name"] = "Venomous Sacrifice", ["text"] = "Channeled (0 sec cast)" }
entries[1301654] = { ["name"] = "Cursed Sanguithorn", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nOnce only usable as an edible plant for fleeting magical power, recent evolutionary changes and alchemical breakthroughs with bloodthistle have led to its use across the professions. This more potent growth has come to be known as sanguithorn, and still boasts fearsome magical capabilities.\n\nSanguithorn are known to tether themselves to rocks, either above or under the ground, so check for them in more rugged terrain.\n\nThe herb gives off a sinister aura as if the very roots are laced with malice. Gathering the plant will surely bring some relief to the land, but at what cost to the herbalist?" }
entries[1301655] = { ["name"] = "Cursed Tranquility Bloom", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nThe environmental factors and changes of Quel'Thalas and the surrounding regions has had a profound impact on the local flora, including even the humble Peacebloom. It is still a staple of local crafting and is utilized in a wide variety of recipes, and a recent strain that has adapted to those changes has been dubbed Tranquility Bloom.\n\nThe herb gives off a sinister aura as if the very roots are laced with malice. Gathering the plant will surely bring some relief to the land, but at what cost to the herbalist?" }
entries[1301657] = { ["name"] = "Overload Cursed Herb", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n5.3 sec cast\nOverloading a Cursed herb draws out more of the curse within it. Experienced herbalists can hold this curse in their hands, willing it into solid form." }
